# UAT runner for the SIMULATED-GPU kind lane (issue #2358). Thin shim over
# tests/uat/lib/phases.sh, which holds the cloud-agnostic phase
# implementations, and a sibling of tests/uat/kind/run. Invoked phase-by-phase
# from .github/workflows/uat-kind-sim.yaml so per-phase failures surface in the
# GitHub Actions UI.
#
# Why this is a separate shim from tests/uat/kind/run rather than a flag on it:
# the two lanes describe DIFFERENT CLUSTERS, and every difference below is a
# property of the cluster, not of the invocation.
#
#   tests/uat/kind/run   single-node, single real H100, nvkind on a self-hosted
#                        GPU runner. Census skipped (one node, no pool that can
#                        grow); TrainJob pinned to one node.
#   this file            four real kind workers with MOCKED NVML devices
#                        (tests/uat/kind/bootstrap-cluster.sh) on a
#                        GitHub-hosted runner. The Slurm block topology needs
#                        four schedulable nodes, and simulated GPUs need no
#                        hardware, so the lane takes no reservation.
#
# The GPU-node census (#2096) is ENFORCED here rather than skipped. On the
# nvkind lane it is opt-out because a single fixed node cannot grow and does
# not carry the cloud lanes' nodeGroup label. Here the count is exactly the
# lane's premise -- four labelled workers -- so asserting it turns "the GPU
# simulation only took on three of the four nodes" into a named failure at the
# readiness gate instead of a wrong topology three phases later.
#
# No CUJ phase runs on this lane: cuj_phase_for returns `none` for a slurm
# platform, because a TrainJob would go to the Kubernetes scheduler and bypass
# slurmd. The workflow invokes prep, install, conformance and verify only.
#
# THE DEPLOYMENT VALIDATION PHASE IS NOT RUN ON THIS LANE, and that is a
# decision. It also DIVERGES from the cloud lanes (uat-aws/gcp/azure), which run
# `--phase all` and gate on the deployment phase; do not "restore" it here
# without reading this.
#
# The lane deploys a SUBSET of its recipe: gpu-operator and nvidia-dra-driver-gpu
# are excluded, because both need a driver stack on the node that a stock
# kindest/node does not have (the full reasoning is in the header of
# tests/uat/kind/tests/h100-training-slurm-config.yaml). `aicr validate`
# validates the RECIPE, not the deployed subset, and offers no component filter,
# so the deployment phase evaluates checks about both excluded components.
#
# It does not merely fail; it cannot finish. `expected-resources` calls
# verifyGPUReadinessSignals, which sees nvidia-dra-driver-gpu declared and polls
# verifyDRAKubeletPluginReady for a DaemonSet that will never be created. That
# poll's zero-match case is deliberately a POLL rather than a fast fail
# (validators/deployment/expected_resources.go: "the DaemonSet's pods churn to
# 0/0 across a GPU-node reboot, which the dwell is there to ride through"), and
# it runs to defaults.GPUReadinessTimeout, 8 minutes, which is exactly the
# validator Job's own deadline. Measured: `aicr validate --phase deployment`
# returned 8 after 574s with 4/4 validators failed and expected-resources killed
# at its deadline, having logged nothing past namespace verification. The
# readiness gate retries that until READINESS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, so keeping it
# would burn 60 minutes to reach the same answer.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS, stated so nobody has to infer it: THIS LANE DOES NOT ASSERT
# DEPLOYMENT READINESS, and a deployment-readiness regression will not be caught
# here. That is the second thing the lane does not cover, alongside the GPU
# stack itself.
#
# IT ALSO SKIPS THE LEAF'S OWN INLINE healthCheckAsserts, which is not obvious
# and matters for #2358. They are dispatched by `expected-resources`
# (validators/deployment/expected_resources.go, the only consumer of
# HealthCheckAsserts in the tree), and that is a deployment-phase check. So the
# topology assertion carried in the recipe does not run here. It is still
# covered hermetically by TestSlurmTopologyHealthCheckClusterStates, and live by
# any consumer that runs `aicr validate --phase deployment` against a full
# deployment of this recipe.
#
# WHAT STILL GATES THE LANE: the conformance phase, which carries
# slinky-slurm-health, and tests/uat/kind/verify-topology.sh as a workflow step
# with the conformance job gated on it. That step is what holds the #2358
# acceptance bar here: it derives the expected block membership from the live
# cluster rather than from the recipe, so it is unaffected by which validator
# phases run. Without it, scoping the validation would have removed the
# acceptance gate altogether.
#
# The leaf declares no performance phase, so `conformance` is everything this
# lane can satisfy.
#
# WHY A SHELL KNOB AND NOT `spec.validate.execution.phases`, which AICRConfig
# does have (pkg/config/config.go ValidateExecutionSpec.Phases): that field only
# reaches the conformance run. install_readiness_gate builds its own invocation
# with `--phase deployment` on the command line, which overrides the config, so
# setting the field alone would narrow the conformance run and leave the gate
# polling. One knob that drives both keeps them from disagreeing; two would
# invite exactly the half-fix this note exists to prevent.
#
# The assignment itself sits with the other exported knobs below.
#
# Usage:
#   AICR_BIN=./aicr RUN_ID=12345 ./run-sim <phase> <test-config.yaml>
# See tests/uat/lib/phases.sh for the phase list and the working files produced.

set -euo pipefail

SIM_SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"

# The cluster shape: WORKER_CLIQUE_MAP (via worker_indices) and the mock-node
# label the device plugin selects on. Sourced rather than restated so a fifth
# worker is a one-file change; the file touches no cluster when sourced.
# shellcheck source=./setup-gpu-sim.sh
source "${SIM_SCRIPT_DIR}/setup-gpu-sim.sh"

# Census contract (see tests/uat/lib/phases.sh, GPU-node census guard). Both
# halves are derived from the constants the labeller itself used: the selector
# from the label it applies, the count from the map it iterates. A literal
# here would go stale the moment the cluster changed shape, and it would go
# stale SILENTLY -- an expectation of 4 against a 5-worker cluster fails
# closed, but an expectation of 4 against a cluster that now has 4 GPU nodes
# for a different reason passes for the wrong one.
GPU_CENSUS_SELECTOR="${MOKKA_NODE_TYPE_LABEL}=${MOKKA_NODE_TYPE}"
EXPECTED_GPU_NODES="$(worker_indices | wc -l | tr -d ' ')"

# Narrows `aicr validate` to the phases this lane can satisfy, and with it turns
# off the post-install readiness gate. The header says why at length, and what it
# costs. Set here rather than in the workflow so a LOCAL run of this shim behaves
# exactly like CI: a knob that only CI sets is a knob whose effect nobody
# reproduces.
VALIDATE_PHASES="conformance"

export GPU_CENSUS_SELECTOR EXPECTED_GPU_NODES VALIDATE_PHASES

# shellcheck source=../lib/phases.sh
source "${SIM_SCRIPT_DIR}/../lib/phases.sh"

uat_main "$@"
